  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Acquired primary cholesteatoma...):</strong> Acquired primary cholesteatomas develop due to chronic Eustachian tube dysfunction producing deep pars flaccida retraction pockets (Bezold's theory) in a perforated/retracted drum.<br>• <strong>Option C (Keratosis obturans...):</strong> Keratosis obturans is a plug of desquamated keratin causing canal widening and severe otalgia in the external auditory canal, not a mass behind an intact drum.<br>• <strong>Option D (Glomus tympanicum...):</strong> Glomus tympanicum is a red/purple vascular paraganglioma presenting with pulsatile tinnitus, not a white, asymptomatic epidermal pearly cyst."
