  level: "Moderate",
  q: "A 58-year-old male presents with progressive, unilateral left-sided nasal obstruction, epistaxis, and hyposmia. Anterior rhinoscopy shows a firm, lobulated, fleshy, reddish-pink polypoid mass originating from the lateral nasal wall around the middle meatus. Biopsy of the lesion reveals non-keratinizing squamous epithelium that inverts and proliferates downward into the underlying stroma, keeping an intact basement membrane. Which of the following features is a major clinical concern regarding this lesion?",
