  exp: "The patient has primary Atrophic Rhinitis (Ozena), characterized by progressive atrophy of the nasal mucosa, ciliated epithelium (metaplasia to squamous), and turbinate bone, with crusting and foul odor caused by saprophytic bacteria (Klebsiella ozaenae). Despite markedly widened, spacious nasal cavities, patients paradoxical experience a sensation of nasal obstruction because airflow receptors in the nasal mucosa are lost. Young's operation involves complete surgical closure of both nostrils (vestibular closure) with flap advancement for 6 to 12 months, allowing the atrophied respiratory epithelium to regenerate in a humid environment. In modified Young's operation, a partial closure is performed to maintain a small airway.",
  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Caldwell-Luc operation):</strong> The Caldwell-Luc procedure provides access to the maxillary sinus through the canine fossa; it is not used to narrow a spacious nasal cavity in atrophic rhinitis.<br>• <strong>Option C (Lothrop's procedure):</strong> The modified Lothrop (Draf III) procedure is an extensive frontal sinusotomy connecting bilateral frontal sinus ostia across the midline, used for refractory frontal sinus disease.<br>• <strong>Option D (Denker's operation):</strong> Denker's operation is a radical open approach uniting the Caldwell-Luc incision with the pyriform aperture for access to benign or malignant anterior skull base tumors."
