  exp: "The patient presents with Granulomatosis with Polyangiitis (GPA, formerly Wegener's Granulomatosis), a systemic necrotizing granulomatous vasculitis involving the classic triad of the upper respiratory tract (nasal crusting, septal perforation, saddle nose deformity), lower respiratory tract (cavitary pulmonary nodules), and kidneys (crescentic necrotizing glomerulonephritis). The pathognomonic serological hallmark is cytoplasmic antineutrophil cytoplasmic antibodies (c-ANCA) directed against Proteinase 3 (PR3), which carries a sensitivity and specificity exceeding 90% to 95% in active generalized disease.",
