  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Within the substance of the palatine tonsillar crypts):</strong> Suppuration within the crypts is chronic follicular tonsillitis or tonsillolithiasis, not an extratonsillar peritonsillar space abscess.<br>• <strong>Option C (In the retropharyngeal space behind the buccopharyngeal fascia):</strong> This defines a retropharyngeal abscess, which produces bulging of the posterior pharyngeal wall and stridor, without unilateral palatal bulging or tonsillar medialization.<br>• <strong>Option D (Between the buccopharyngeal fascia and the alar fascia):</strong> This is the true retropharyngeal space; the danger space lies between the alar and prevertebral fasciae."
