  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Killian-Jamieson space):</strong> Killian-Jamieson space is an anterolateral space located below the cricopharyngeus and lateral to the longitudinal tendon of the esophagus; an outpouching here is a Killian-Jamieson diverticulum.<br>• <strong>Option C (Laimer's triangle):</strong> Laimer's (Laimer-Haeckermann) triangle is a weak area located below the cricopharyngeus muscle on the posterior wall of the cervical esophagus, bounded laterally by the longitudinal muscle fibers of the esophagus.<br>• <strong>Option D (Sinus of Morgagni):</strong> The Sinus of Morgagni is a space between the upper border of the superior pharyngeal constrictor and the skull base transmitting the Eustachian tube, levator veli palatini, and ascending palatine artery."
