  exp: "Laryngomalacia is the most common congenital laryngeal anomaly and the leading cause of congenital inspiratory stridor in infants (accounting for >60% to 70% of cases). It is caused by delayed neuromuscular maturation and flaccidity of the supraglottic cartilaginous structures. On inspiration, the negative intrathoracic and transglottic pressures cause the flaccid supraglottic structures (aryepiglottic folds and an omega-shaped epiglottis) to prolapse inward, creating fluttering inspiratory stridor. Stridor characteristically worsens when supine and improves in the prone position. Most cases are mild and resolve spontaneously by 18 to 24 months of age; severe cases (with failure to thrive or apnea) are treated with endoscopic supraglottoplasty.",
