  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Through the cricoid cartilage and first tracheal ring):</strong> High tracheostomy through the cricoid or 1st ring is strictly avoided because it damages the only complete cartilaginous ring of the airway, resulting in circumferential subglottic stenosis.<br>• <strong>Option C (Between the fifth and sixth tracheal rings):</strong> A low tracheostomy places the cannula dangerously close to the brachiocephalic artery and pleural domes, predisposing to fatal hemorrhage and pneumothorax.<br>• <strong>Option D (Directly through the cricothyroid membrane):</strong> An incision through the cricothyroid membrane is an emergency cricothyroidotomy (coniotomy), performed only for acute 'cannot intubate, cannot ventilate' scenarios; it must be converted to a formal tracheostomy within 24–48 hours."
